{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKit Swift SDK provides a modern async\/await version of the YubiKit framework, making it easy to integrate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Swift and SwiftUI based applications. The async\/await syntax provides an easy to read and powerful way of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"creating connections and sending commands to the different applications on the YubiKey.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()"]},{"style":"warning","type":"aside","name":"Warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This SDK does not perform zeroization of sensitive data in memory. Cryptographic keys, PIN tokens,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and other secrets are not securely erased when no longer in use. This is currently out of scope but may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"addressed in a future release."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"YubiKit","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"YubiKit","modules":[{"name":"YubiKit"}],"platforms":[{"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iOS","beta":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"macOS","beta":false}],"images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"documentation-header.png"}],"color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"green"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit","inte